```csharp
{10.5f, 12.3f}
```
This is because the average front wall height is (10.5 + 11.2 + 9.8) / 3 = 10.5, and the average back wall height is (12.3 + 13.1 + 11.5) / 3 = 12.3.

Your task is to implement the `CalculateAverageHeight` method to achieve this functionality.

code:
public float[] CalculateAverageHeight(float[,] wallHeights)
{
    int rows = wallHeights.GetLength(0);
    int cols = wallHeights.GetLength(1);

    float[] averageHeights = new float[cols];

    for (int col = 0; col < cols; col++)
    {
        float sum = 0;
        for (int row = 0; row < rows; row++)
        {
            sum += wallHeights[row, col];
        }
        averageHeights[col] = sum / rows;
    }

    return averageHeights;
}

